      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2133095443,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This is at least part of #19883. Are there any other offsets or is that all of them?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-27T11:33:16.032Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-27T11:33:16.032Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 330442073,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17457,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "55e82a9967e2efd4a1a8c406a2c2bcbd47828092",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2134185406,
          "type": null,
          "body": "They're the only ones in `mysql_exec_param_offset()`, which is the routine added in  !15863, which is the merge request to which #19883 refers.\n\nIt's not necessarily the only one in the MySQL dissector, much less the only one in Wireshark as a whole.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-27T21:38:38.482Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-27T21:38:38.482Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 330442073,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17457,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7eabf379d60add4acd9b965807212af96a55f6be",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2134195765,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> It's not necessarily the only one in the MySQL dissector\n\nThere's one outside of `mysql_exec_param_offset()` that this change also fixes; it was outside the changes in !15863 (it's the code that handles the NULL bitmap, which we don't dissect, we just skip over it; that's the underlying problem - perhaps we should make it an `FT_BYTES` field, at least, possibly without displaying the value in the protocol tree).\n\nBut there may be more.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-27T21:53:02.174Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-27T21:53:02.174Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 330442073,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17457,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ec4190dc8640dd5ab9505cfeb0eb29c8557f88c4",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2134196699,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Certainly in Wireshark as a whole: The Monero dissector has the one cast away by 804daf03dfa9946e05283eafb8539d7a3468364a, which ultimately stems from `tcp_dissect_pdus` not expecting PDUs with lengths larger than 32 bit integers.\n\nActually finding all of them would be a challenge. But I suppose #19883 as a specific issue, as opposed to the issue in Wireshark as a whole, is fixed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-27T21:55:10.466Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-27T21:55:10.466Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 330442073,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17457,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -2479,9 +2479,15 @@ mysql_exec_param_offset(tvbuff_t *tvb, proto_tree *req_tree, int offset, int par\n \tuint64_t param_length;\n \n \tfor (int i = 0; i<param_count; i++) {\n-\t\toffset += 2; // param type\n+\t\t// param type\n+\t\ttvb_ensure_bytes_exist(tvb, offset, 2);\n+\t\toffset += 2;\n+\t\t// param length\n \t\tlenfle = tvb_get_fle(tvb, req_tree, offset, &param_length, NULL);\n-\t\toffset += lenfle + (int)param_length;\n+\t\toffset += lenfle;\n+\t\t// param data\n+\t\ttvb_ensure_bytes_exist(tvb, offset, (int)param_length);\n+\t\toffset += (int)param_length;\n \t}\n \n \treturn offset;\n@@ -2855,7 +2861,11 @@ mysql_dissect_request(tvbuff_t *tvb,packet_info *pinfo, int offset, proto_tree *\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\tif (param_count != 0) {\n \t\t\t\tuint8_t stmt_bound;\n-\t\t\t\toffset += (int)(param_count + 7) / 8; /* NULL bitmap */\n+\t\t\t\tint null_bitmap_length;\n+\t\t\t\t/* NULL bitmap */\n+\t\t\t\tnull_bitmap_length = (int)((param_count + 7) / 8);\n+\t\t\t\ttvb_ensure_bytes_exist(tvb, offset, null_bitmap_length);\n+\t\t\t\toffset += null_bitmap_length;\n \t\t\t\tproto_tree_add_item(req_tree, hf_mysql_new_parameter_bound_flag, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_NA);\n \t\t\t\tstmt_bound = tvb_get_uint8(tvb, offset);\n \t\t\t\toffset += 1;\n",
